Q) Does below mutate original array

   ```JS
     users
    .filter(user => user.age > 30)
    .sort((a, b) => a.age - b.age)
  ```
    A) Yes — .sort() mutates the array it’s called on.
    However my above answer DOESNOT mutate original array
  because filter() creates a new array first, and then sort() mutates that new filtered array.
    More safer way 
    
    ```JS    
      const sorted = [...users].sort((a, b) => a.age - b.age);
    ```JS    
   
    ## in nutshell:
    ```JS
        users.sort(...) → mutates users
        users.filter(...).sort(...) → mutates only the filtered result, not users
        ```JS

